# rule.require.rules-are-clusters

a rule is a cluster, not a file that accretes.

```
rule.forbid.$topic.md                 # the CLASS — lean entry point
rule.forbid.$topic.example=$id.md     # ONE file per occurrence — opt-in
```

the rule keeps exactly one worked case, the sharpest. every other occurrence, and the full record of the worked one (sweep, injections, residual), goes to an example file beside it.

one file per occurrence; the id in the filename is the citation:

```
👍  rule.forbid.$topic.example=R9-U1.md
👎  rule.forbid.$topic.example=occurrences.md
```

the rule's `.see also` points down, one line each, stating what sets that occurrence apart:

```md
- `rule.forbid.$topic.example=R9-U1.md`  — the 2026-08-09 sweep, 14 injections, 1 residual
```

test: does this paragraph describe the mechanism, or one time it fired? mechanism → rule · one time → example · no worked case at all → keep the sharpest one.

blocker: second worked case added to a rule file rather than ejected · occurrences collapsed into one `example=occurrences.md`.
nitpick: example with no `.see also` pointer from its rule · rule with zero worked cases.

⇒ `rule.require.catalog-is-an-index`
